    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20532" root="سلم" body-key="s">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تسلّم مِنْهُ</span></b>  <i>He asserted,</i> or <i>declared, himself
to be free from,</i> or <i>clear of,</i> or <i>quit of, it,</i> or
<i>him.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تسلّم</span> is also <i>syn.</i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُسْلَمَ</span>, in two
senses: see the latter, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تسلّمهُ</span> signifies <i>He took it,</i> or <i>received it;</i> namely,
a thing given, or delivered. (S, M, Msb, K.)

